WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:03.608
Now we are going to
answer some fan questions.

00:00:03.608 --> 00:00:04.441
Yes.

00:00:04.441 --> 00:00:05.274
Is that okay, you ready?

00:00:05.274 --> 00:00:06.107
Yes it is.

00:00:06.107 --> 00:00:07.631
All right, great.

00:00:07.631 --> 00:00:11.114
Firsthand question from
@bennyfactor, on Twitter,

00:00:11.114 --> 00:00:15.281
asks, "Do you prefer San
Pellegrino or Perrier

00:00:15.309 --> 00:00:17.148
"or some other sparkling mineral water

00:00:17.148 --> 00:00:19.192
"that we've never heard of?"

00:00:19.192 --> 00:00:21.393
@bennyfactor, on Twitter,

00:00:21.393 --> 00:00:24.330
asks what kind of sparkling
water do I prefer.

00:00:24.330 --> 00:00:28.497
Well, in fact, benny, the
answer is quite complex.

00:00:28.538 --> 00:00:30.041
It differs according to my mood.

00:00:30.041 --> 00:00:31.085
I can tell you this.

00:00:31.085 --> 00:00:33.910
If I am drinking sparkling
water on it's own,

00:00:33.910 --> 00:00:36.450
I might prefer San Pellegrino,

00:00:36.450 --> 00:00:38.876
which is an Italian sparkling water.

00:00:38.876 --> 00:00:43.043
I like San Pellegrino
under that circumstance.

00:00:43.274 --> 00:00:45.794
I could tell you that my
favorite sparkling water

00:00:45.794 --> 00:00:49.961
to drink after espresso is
the German Gerolsteiner water,

00:00:50.215 --> 00:00:52.236
which is quite a freak of nature.

00:00:52.236 --> 00:00:54.889
The mineral content is so incredibly high,

00:00:54.889 --> 00:00:58.790
over 2,000 parts per million
total dissolved solids,

00:00:58.790 --> 00:01:02.957
also known as TDS and the
mineral content is so high,

00:01:03.400 --> 00:01:06.705
in fact, that if you were
to drink a Liter of it a day

00:01:06.705 --> 00:01:07.922
you would have a quarter

00:01:07.922 --> 00:01:10.331
of your daily requirement of magnesium.

00:01:10.331 --> 00:01:13.306
And magnesium is a very
difficult mineral to obtain.

00:01:13.306 --> 00:01:16.306
Supplementing orally is inefficient.

00:01:17.584 --> 00:01:20.620
I rub magnesium lotion all over my body

00:01:20.620 --> 00:01:23.334
to make use of transdermal absorption.

00:01:23.334 --> 00:01:25.537
People don't understand;
sometimes they use

00:01:25.537 --> 00:01:28.149
artificial products that
they rub on their skin,

00:01:28.149 --> 00:01:30.657
like certain sunscreens
and lotions and they say,

00:01:30.657 --> 00:01:32.483
"It's okay, I'm not eating
it, it's on my skin",

00:01:32.483 --> 00:01:33.736
but whatever you put on your skin

00:01:33.736 --> 00:01:35.036
goes into your bloodstream.

00:01:35.036 --> 00:01:37.747
For example, people wearing nicotine patch

00:01:37.747 --> 00:01:40.580
and other medication patches for a

00:01:41.607 --> 00:01:43.529
very direct absorption to the bloodstream.

00:01:43.529 --> 00:01:47.133
For example, cavemen used to
swim in the ocean all the time

00:01:47.133 --> 00:01:49.024
and the ocean is a rich
source of magnesium.

00:01:49.024 --> 00:01:50.498
That transdermal exposure

00:01:50.498 --> 00:01:52.996
gave the cavemen the
magnesium they needed.

00:01:52.996 --> 00:01:55.415
Now swimming in the ocean
has fallen out of favor

00:01:55.415 --> 00:01:59.582
for most of us and therefore
other methods are necessary.

00:01:59.812 --> 00:02:01.856
Organ meats have also fallen out of favor,

00:02:01.856 --> 00:02:04.680
another rich dietary source of magnesium.

00:02:04.680 --> 00:02:07.136
Nevertheless, Gerolsteiner, to me,

00:02:07.136 --> 00:02:11.303
has such a dense minerality
that perfectly suits

00:02:11.811 --> 00:02:14.238
the bitter complexity that you get

00:02:14.238 --> 00:02:17.143
from drinking an espresso.

00:02:17.143 --> 00:02:21.076
Wow, okay, do you just
get it from the internet.?

00:02:21.076 --> 00:02:22.922
The great thing about Gerolsteiner

00:02:22.922 --> 00:02:24.588
is it's so readily available.

00:02:24.588 --> 00:02:27.525
It can be found at
every Trader Joe's store

00:02:27.525 --> 00:02:28.386
that I've been to.

00:02:28.386 --> 00:02:30.013
It can be found at Whole Foods.

00:02:30.013 --> 00:02:34.180
I think it costs $1.49 at Trader
Joe, $1.69 at whole foods.

00:02:35.327 --> 00:02:36.526
Oh my God.

00:02:36.526 --> 00:02:39.542
However, if you buy a
case of Gerolsteiner water

00:02:39.542 --> 00:02:42.874
at Whole Foods they
give you anunadvertised

00:02:42.874 --> 00:02:46.125
10% case discount, bringing the price down

00:02:46.125 --> 00:02:47.708
17 cents per Liter.

